{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Check a Tesla VIN"},"description":"Check a used Tesla by its VIN. Use it when someone gives you a 17-character Tesla VIN, for example from a listing. From Tesla's own record for that car it returns whether Full Self-Driving is on it, the Autopilot computer, the battery pack and the build date. It also returns the model, model year and plant from the VIN, the number of NHTSA recalls and of Tesla's service bulletins for the model year, and links for the person. On free Supercharging it gives the rule for a car that cannot have it. For a Model S or Model X built before April 2017 it says the answer is in the paid Factory Report, with that report's link. For a Model S of 2012 to 2016 or a 2016 Model X it also returns the paid Service Report, which goes through those service bulletins for the car, with its link and a sample. It does not cover battery health, accidents, title history or mileage. Read-only and free, within a daily limit.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"vin":{"description":"The car's 17-character VIN, as on the listing or the label in the driver's door frame.","type":"string"}},"required":["vin"],"type":"object"},"name":"check_tesla_vin","outputSchema":{"oneOf":[{"properties":{"ok":{"const":true}},"required":["ok","vin","car","identity","full_self_driving","autopilot_computer","battery_pack","built","free_supercharging","recalls","report","not_included","links"],"type":"object"},{"properties":{"ok":{"const":false}},"required":["ok","error","message"],"type":"object"}],"properties":{"autopilot_computer":{"properties":{"answer":{"type":"string"},"read_on":{"type":"string"},"source":{"const":"Tesla's record","type":"string"}},"required":["answer","source"],"type":"object"},"battery_pack":{"properties":{"answer":{"type":"string"},"read_on":{"type":"string"},"source":{"const":"Tesla's record","type":"string"}},"required":["a